  "rationale": "structural: The only structural obligation in the subject text is the prescribed signature: `Criterion::source_node_id` is a method of `pub trait Criterion<D: Domain>` that takes `&self` and returns `NodeId<D>`. An alternative that returns the node some other way would break this. Examples are a free function, an associated const, a method returning `Option<NodeId<D>>`, or a method taking `self` by value. The sentence that the method identifies the criterion's source node is observable behavior. It is satisfied by each implementing type's return value, so it adds no further structural clause. The root `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#trait[Criterion]/fn[source_node_id]` declares exactly `fn source_node_id(&self) -> NodeId<D>;` inside the `Criterion<D>` trait, and it carries the `{impl}` marker for this requirement. That covers the signature obligation. Which trait the method belongs to, and the supertrait bounds, belong to the parent `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`, not to this subject.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement's only behavioral obligation is that `Criterion::source_node_id` identifies the criterion's source node. The marked test `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` covers it.\n\n- The test criterion `Review` has `new`, which sets `source` to `intern_node(Node(1))`. Its `Criterion::source_node_id` returns that `source`.\n- The test runs `validator.verify(descriptor())` and asserts `value.source_node_id() == &domain.cache().intern_node(Node(1))`. That checks the node the criterion reports comes through as the produced value's source node.\n- The test saves the value and loads it back. It asserts `loaded.source_node_id() == value.source_node_id()`, so the persisted identity is kept. The load also succeeds only when the record is keyed by the criterion's source node.\n- Other tests use a different source node. `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` sets `future.source` to `Node(2)` and asserts that no evidence is loaded. This shows the source node taken from the criterion is what distinguishes records.\n\nI found no obligation without a test. The test is the marked one, and no marking gap exists. Only the tests named above were checked, and no implementation source was needed.",
